Probe build only: make the pair-table row count and the scan block settable
from the environment, so the true cost of each can be measured at every cell.
NEVER a tournament arm -- a measured arm's row count and block are fixed
functions of the public parameters, decided before any probe is drawn, and an
environment variable is neither. With none of the three variables set the
shipped rules are bit-for-bit unchanged, and every sweep below checks that
against the frozen `orbits` worker before it measures anything.

  IC_TABLE_ROWS  the pair-table row count        (round18_row_sweep.py)
  IC_SCAN_CEIL   the ceiling in the block clamp  (round18_block_sweep.py)
  IC_SCAN_BLOCK  the scan block outright         (round18_block_grid.py)

`IC_SCAN_CEIL` can only lower a block below what the rule asks for, which is
why `IC_SCAN_BLOCK` exists: at the cells whose rule value is already the floor
of 8, the ceiling cannot move the block at all, and choosing a constant needs
the whole grid.

Apply to a copy of `runs/round-0017/source_candidates/orbits/source`:

    cp -a runs/round-0017/source_candidates/orbits/source /tmp/probe18
    patch -d /tmp/probe18 -p1 -i "$PWD/campaign_20260916/round18-rows-probe.patch"
    ( cd /tmp/probe18 && cargo build --release --example ic_tournament_worker )

The build must happen inside the tree: a --manifest-path build would not pick
up the snapshot's .cargo/config.toml, which selects the musl static target.

